    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d218-a1-a2-a5">

                <pb facs="0485" n="465" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg465"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">United States District Attorney to her Majesty’s
                        Vice-Consul.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Attorney’s Office,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Key West,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-07-15"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 15, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> The master of the British schooner lately
                    sent into this port as prize called the Don José, request me to state that no
                    proceedings have been instituted against the vessel. Such is the fact. On a
                    thorough examination of the ship’s papers, and the depositions of the witnesses
                    examined, I am unable to find any facts which warrant her detention; and I have
                    no objection to her going to sea at any time.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>THOMAS J. BOYNTON, <hi rendition="#italic">United States Attorney,</hi>
                    </signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph B. Browne</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting British Vice-Consul.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
